   "line": [
    "Nd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Tradition held that the forward knight retreat was practically the only move, but a popular modern alternative is to drop the knight all the way home to d7. It looks like nothing special, yet it neatly covers the pin — the central capture no longer works, since the pawn can be taken or the knight grabbed and the position held with a pawn move.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 164,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pppn1ppp/2n5/1B1pP3/3p4/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQ1RK1 b kq - 3 7",
